# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A method that reads a free name forms its own value of it, and that value
# is what its callees receive; a method that only hands the name on forms
# nothing. mk's formal n is a free name of the definition f it returns: u5
# holds f with n 5. No caller anywhere has an n. g, made with n 70, reads n
# and calls u5: g's own value, 70, read from its node, is the value f
# receives: 70 and 71. h, made with n 70 as well, does not read n and only
# calls u5: nothing is formed, and f reads its own 5: 6. w, made with n 70,
# adds 2 to its n and calls u5: 72 and 73, and again 72 and 73: the
# assignment changes the value of that activation and neither node. After
# all of them f's own n is still 5: 6. Entry 7.
fn: mk (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: f () int
        return: n + 1
    return: f

@: u5 mk(5)

fn: mkreads (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: g () int
        return: n * 1000 + u5()
    return: g

fn: mkhands (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: h () int
        return: u5()
    return: h

fn: mkwrites (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: w () int
        n: n + 2
        return: n * 1000 + u5()
    return: w

@: vg mkreads(70)
@: vh mkhands(70)
@: vw mkwrites(70)
int: a vg()
int: b vh()
int: c vw()
int: d vw()
int: e u5()
int: ok 7
if: a != 70071 || b != 6 || c != 72073 || d != 72073 || e != 6
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
